  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c **** /**
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * @brief Dot product of Q7 vectors.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcA points to the first input vector
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * @param[in]       *pSrcB points to the second input vector
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * @param[in]       blockSize number of samples in each vector
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * @param[out]      *result output result returned here
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * @return none.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  *
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * \par
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * The intermediate multiplications are in 1.7 x 1.7 = 2.14 format and these
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * results are added to an accumulator in 18.14 format.
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * Nonsaturating additions are used and there is no danger of wrap around as long as
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * the vectors are less than 2^18 elements long.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  * The return result is in 18.14 format.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c ****  */
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/BasicMathFunctions/arm_dot_prod_q7.c **** 
